\f0\fs24 \cf0 README\
\
This dataset accompanies the open-access paper \'93Who knows, who cares? Untangling ecological knowledge and nature connection among Amazonian colonist farmers. The data was collected in the form of questionnaires in 2016 among farmers living along the Transamazon Highway in the municipalities of Uruar\'e1, Medicil\'e2ndia, Brasil Novo, and Altamira. It contains information on the farmers\'92 recognition of select species of local wild birds based on photos, sound recordings and sound-image matching, farmers psychological connection with nature, indicative of having a sense of care about the natural world, and a number of factors that could be influencing ecological knowledge and nature connection.\
\
Full description of the variables and data processing used is included in the paper and the supplementary material. Here, we only provide a key to the included variables.\
                       \
Note that in the interest of preserving respondents\'92 anonymity, the dataset presented here compared to that used in the study was transformed as follows: data on education and distance from the main urban centre have been removed, age was grouped into age groups, and distance to nearest market town was converted from km to equidistant categories \'91near, \'91mid-range\'92 and \'91far\'92. If you need access to the full original dataset, please enter in contact with the corresponding author to discuss it.\
